# part: A4 - one program, many interpreters (pure interpreter)
# dir: a4/handin
# load: :m + APL.AST APL.Eval APL.InterpPure
? Print is an EFFECT now. Where does the text come out in a PURE interpreter?
runEval (eval (Print "hello" (CstInt 1)))
? Two prints inside one Add: in which order, and why is that guaranteed?
runEval (eval (Add (Print "a" (CstInt 1)) (Print "b" (CstInt 2))))
? Put then get on the same key
runEval (eval (Let "x" (KvPut (CstInt 0) (CstInt 7)) (KvGet (CstInt 0))))
? QB section 4 Q7: a transaction that fails after a KvPut
runEval (eval (Transaction (Let "x" (KvPut (CstInt 0) (CstInt 1)) (Div (CstInt 1) (CstInt 0)))))
? ... so after that transaction, what is in key 0?
runEval (eval (Let "t" (TryCatch (Transaction (Let "x" (KvPut (CstInt 0) (CstInt 1)) (Div (CstInt 1) (CstInt 0)))) (CstInt 0)) (KvGet (CstInt 0))))
? A transaction that succeeds, and a print inside it
runEval (eval (Let "t" (Transaction (Print "inside" (KvPut (CstInt 0) (CstInt 9)))) (KvGet (CstInt 0))))
? QB section 4 Q6: Break out of a loop from inside a lambda
runEval (eval (ForLoop ("p", CstInt 0) ("i", CstInt 10) (Apply (Lambda "x" (Break (Var "i"))) (CstInt 0))))
